<p style="margin:0 0 8px;">Hi <%= recipientName %>,</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">Your rollback of restore <strong style="color:#0f172a;"><%= label %></strong>, sourced from backup <strong style="color:#0f172a;"><%= backupConfigName %></strong>, has failed.</p>

<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="background-color:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:13px 18px;font-size:13px;color:#64748b;">Rollback job ID</td>
    <td style="padding:13px 18px;font-size:13px;color:#0f172a;font-weight:600;text-align:right;"><%= restoreJobId %></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<% if (errorMessage) { %>
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin-top:14px;">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:13px 16px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:#b91c1c;background-color:#fef2f2;border:1px solid #fecaca;border-radius:8px;"><%= errorMessage %></td>
  </tr>
</table>
<% } %>

<p style="margin:20px 0 0;">Unlike a restore, a rollback undoes changes already made to your CRM — since it didn't finish, some records may be in a partially rolled-back state. Please review the affected records before retrying, or reach out if this keeps happening.</p>
